EXACT-HASH REVIEW — NO ACK OF REVISION 2.

I verified the published artifact on disk:

  path    docs/plans/2026-09-01-recall-construction-prd.md
  bytes   36095
  sha256  b69819b85fd03955505a5a836b50d2560392d00447f97b59d27b87da6f75a618
  state   untracked

Revision 2 closes the original V1-V4 blockers and corrects R11.7 honestly. It is not yet ACK-ready. V5/V6 contain four scientific contradictions, and the Owner/CEO external review identifies a separate missing PRODUCT layer that cannot be dismissed as scope creep in a file calling itself a PRD.

A. FOUR BLOCKERS IN THESE EXACT BYTES

A1. R3’S POSITIVE CONTROL MAKES AUTHENTICITY IMPLY ADMISSION

R3.5 correctly says conformance, authenticity, and scientific admission do not imply one another. Court R3-FORGED then says the same artifact “under an admitted trust root” makes all three mint.

A trust root establishes authenticity. It does not establish the use-specific scientific admission predicate. An authentic provider can be scientifically inadmissible for the named use.

Required controls are four, not three:

- internally conformant, forged/unverified authority: conformance yes; authenticity no/unverified; admission requiring it no;
- internally conformant, authentic, but use-inadmissible: conformance yes; authenticity yes; scientific admission no;
- internally conformant, authentic, and use-admissible: all required witnesses mint;
- plain checksum: no upgrade beyond whatever internal conformance is actually replayed.

Replace “under an admitted trust root → all three” with separate authenticity and admission controls.

A2. R4 CELL 8 REINTRODUCES THE MONOTONICITY CLAIM THE THREAD REJECTED

Revision 2 requires support for latent gap 412 to be equal or lower when the same call emits extra nearby gaps. One-to-one matching does not prove that. Summing over associations can add a lawful match to a second latent boundary or alter hypothesis-relative odds; a normalized clutter/count law may raise or lower a score depending on competing H.

The model-independent invariant is narrower:

- redundant detections within one call do not increment admitted INDEPENDENT-source count;
- they cannot independently satisfy a provider-agreement threshold;
- at most one observation matches one latent boundary in one association;
- likelihood/posterior changes are exactly those prescribed by the frozen normalized clutter/count/dependence model;
- the two-boundary positive remains recoverable.

Remove “support MUST NOT increase.” Keep a frozen model-specific numerical oracle only after Q-A2 exists.

Also generalize R4.7 as Owner/CEO recommends: ONE PROVIDER CALL IS ONE JOINT OBSERVATION. A point set is one observation form, not the universal provider contract. Region sets, gap fields, ranked plans, posterior samples, and structured charts must not be flattened and stripped of dependence. Likewise the calibration target is a declared target object—exact plan, acceptable plans, regions, annotator distribution, or task-loss target—not always one latent exact plan.

A3. R7’S NAMED 2x2 VIOLATES R2/R9 BY MAKING CELLS EQUAL CLAIMS

The fixture refuses (PA,IY) because “two predicates cannot bind inside one cell that asserts a single claim” and refuses (PB,IX) because “a predicate cannot be bisected ... by a cell boundary.”

Those are precisely the conflations R2 and R9 were written to prevent:

- a cell is a contiguous computational carrier, not a claim;
- multiple claims may share one cell/span;
- one claim may have overlapping or discontinuous support and may cross cell boundaries;
- cell-to-semantic-artifact incidence is potentially many-to-many.

Revision 2’s court would prohibit lawful semantics to make its matrix come out clean.

Owner/CEO’s “cells are not claims” requirement is therefore not optional polish. Add it as a normative architecture law before attempting R7 fixtures:

- cell plans never define the semantic inventory or claim count;
- semantic artifacts/discourse acts may overlap, be discontinuous, and cross cells;
- incidence is many-to-many;
- no duplication or deletion follows merely from touching zero/one/many cells;
- a fixed-view projection records any semantic information it cannot represent.

R7 compatibility then proves subject/coordinate/eligibility/incidence/relation/projection laws. A safer first 2x2 uses two transcript derivations or coordinate dialects and two interpretations whose evidence is bound to those derivations: matching pairs admit; cross pairs refuse or remain unresolved unless a validated crosswalk exists. It does not manufacture one-claim-per-cell semantics.

A4. R10 IS A SINGLE ENUM THAT COLLAPSES C5, AND ITS OWN COURT IS UNREACHABLE

BaselineHeuristic | ProviderResolved | Adjudicated | AuthorityAbsent mixes:

- construction route;
- resolver outcome;
- provider authenticity;
- adjudication route;
- calibration;
- scientific admission;
- segmentation conditioning.

C5 explicitly says these remain independently represented. ProviderResolved is especially false: providers propose; the deterministic resolver resolves. Adjudicated authenticates neither the adjudicator nor scientific admissibility.

R10.2 also says the enum is derived only from an R3.5 witness and no witness means AuthorityAbsent. Its court nevertheless expects direct RecallSegmenter—which has no such witness—to derive BaselineHeuristic. Both cannot hold.

Current source shows the real consumer hazard:

- InterviewSegmenter.Segmented has graph/turnOf/crossing, no construction standing.
- BenchCase accepts any RecallGraph[Checked]; inputChecksum omits construction route/authority.
- CaseRun carries recallChecksum only.
- BenchReport.label can emit and render CALIBRATED solely from frozen-set/protocol state.

So benchmark calibration can coexist with heuristic segmentation while the rendered report exposes one flattering “CALIBRATED” headline.

Replace the enum with independently derived facts, whose prose badge is only a projection:

- executed construction route + recipe/code/config identity;
- conformance state;
- authenticity state/trust-root receipt;
- calibration basis;
- adjudication protocol/basis;
- use-specific admission;
- conditioning plan identities and per-estimand segmentation-conditioned status;
- subject binding.

The direct baseline route is established by the executing recipe, not inferred from missing metadata. Missing route remains unknown/authority-absent. Each coordinate binds into durable identity. Bench calibration and recall-construction standing remain simultaneously visible.

B. PROVENANCE CORRECTION

The header says measured against adf58cad/6ec8b698 plus unspecified archive probes, and §H says “All on adf58cad / 6ec8b698.” The chief’s shipped-fingerprint falsifier was measured on d147b596. Every measured fact needs its exact source SHA and command/receipt. Do not place the d147 result under an “all on” statement naming different commits.

C. ENGAGEMENT WITH OWNER/CEO EXTERNAL REVIEW

I accept the review’s central distinction:

- this document is becoming a strong INTEGRITY / AUTHORITY / ESTIMAND-SAFETY DESIGN CONTRACT;
- it is not yet a complete PRODUCT PRD.

The missing product layer is load-bearing, not a request for cosmetic API examples. Before whole-PRD adoption, a self-contained artifact must define roles—not necessarily final Scala names—for:

1. raw recall observation identity;
2. transcript derivation identity and coordinate crosswalk;
3. eligible-region/cell-plan proposals and their resolution state;
4. semantic interpretation artifacts independent of cells;
5. many-to-many cell/artifact incidence and compatibility witness;
6. complete recall construction with independent C-family facts;
7. construction family/alternatives/search receipt;
8. a named, reversible fixed-view projection to RecallGraph[Checked], with decision/loss policy, alternatives, construction identity, and representation-loss receipt;
9. the exact artifact admitted to alignment;
10. the durable result that carries construction and estimand qualification downstream.

I do NOT endorse the review’s illustrative Scala names as approved vocabulary. I endorse the artifact roles and operations.

I also accept these external-review amendments:

- claim-first semantic carrier law (“cells are not claims”);
- one call = one native joint observation, not necessarily a point set;
- declared calibration-target family, not metaphysical exact-plan truth;
- silent fixed segmentation is forbidden, but a named reversible decision projection under declared loss is lawful;
- raw-observation identity differs from transcript-derivation identity;
- R7 needs formal compatibility laws and many-to-many incidence;
- N5 should say renaming Checked is not required here; any rename must be complete, versioned, courted, and separately authorized—not “out of scope at any size” forever;
- geometry/crosswalk/regrouping laws need generated properties in addition to frozen examples;
- Q-B/P2 needs owner-level corpus, ethics/REB, annotation, budget, freeze, and contamination authority before calibrated milestones are executable.

D. PROPOSED CONSENSUS / DOCUMENT DISPOSITION

Split the decision rather than forcing one 36 KB file to be four documents:

1. RECALL-CONSTRUCTION DESIGN CONTRACT:
   R2/R3/R7/R8/R9 plus corrected R4 observation principles and R11 raw-trace/canonical-projection law.

2. IMMEDIATE HARDENING:
   R1 is independently scopable now.
   R11 courts are executable, but implementation still awaits chief scoping of the acquire/document admission boundary.
   R10 is NOT implementable until A4 is corrected.
   R12 remains a dedicated identity ADR; two-level identity is the leading recommendation, not selected by this review.

3. PRODUCT PRD:
   central artifact roles, end-to-end operations, user-visible refusals/qualifications, modules, fixed-view compatibility projection, first vertical slice, definition of done.

4. STATISTICAL / SCIENTIFIC PROTOCOL:
   Q-A model family, calibration targets, R8 estimand algebra, preregistration, P2, E1-E5.

The first usable vertical slice should not wait for calibration:

  transcript
  -> separately typed heuristic boundary/semantic proposals
  -> authority-explicit construction artifact retaining Unresolved/Alternatives
  -> named fixed RecallGraph view with projection receipt
  -> existing GraphHsmm
  -> result bound to complete construction identity and visibly segmentation-conditioned

That slice provides immediate product value without laundering the baseline as calibrated science.

VERDICT ON b69819b8…a618: substantial correction, no ACK. Fix A1-A4 and choose the document/product disposition above. Do not mutate these bytes and keep the hash: publish revision 3 under a new byte count/hash with zero inherited ACKs.

No implementation, public vocabulary, module, dependency, ADR, bead, path, reservation, merge, or authority selected here.
